<BaseLayout title="Voter Check · Nizam Mohammed" description="Voter Check, a public search of Hyderabad's 2026 draft electoral rolls and the case system volunteers use to help removed voters get back on the roll." headerVariant="internal" activeNav="work">
<article class="project"><a href="/work" class="project__back project__back--top">← Work</a><header class="project__hero"><div class="project__hero-media project__hero-media--shot"><a class="pshot pshot--link" href="https://votercheck.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open Voter Check at votercheck.me"><img src="/project/voter-card.jpg" alt="The Voter Check walkthrough page"><span class="pshot__cue">Visit votercheck.me</span></a></div><div class="project__hero-heading"><h1 class="project__title page-heading-reveal">Voter Check</h1><p class="project__hero-sub">A public search of Hyderabad's 2026 draft electoral rolls, and the case system volunteers use to help removed voters get back on the roll.</p><div class="project__hero-actions"><a class="project__hero-cta" href="https://votercheck.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit the live site</a><span class="project__hero-id">votercheck.me</span></div></div></header><div class="project__meta project__meta--role"><span class="project__status"><span class="project__status-dot project__status-dot--live" aria-hidden="true"></span>Live</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Civic tech</span></div><p class="project__role"><span class="project__role-label">Role</span>Full-stack and ML engineer</p><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">About</p><div class="project__body"><p>In 2026 the Election Commission of India carried out a Special Intensive Revision of Telangana's electoral rolls. The draft roll, published in August 2026, listed about 26.5 million voters, down from about 33.8 million before the revision, leaving about 7.3 million people off the list. A voter left off has to file a form within a short, fixed window to be added back. The official rolls are published only as scanned images with no text layer, so an ordinary person cannot easily search them.</p><p>Voter Check is a public website built as volunteer work for Young Voice of India, a non-profit whose volunteers help people left off the list to file the form and get back on the roll. It covers 17 Hyderabad-area assembly constituencies and has two parts. The first is a public search anyone can use to find their own record. The second is the case system volunteers and coordinators use to carry each request through to a filed Form 6.</p><p class="rdlink__lead">Across the 15 constituencies where both the draft roll and the removed-voter list are published, about 1.9 million of some 4.7 million electors reviewed were removed, about 41 percent. The analysis reports counts and rates only, with no claim about why any name was removed.</p><a class="paper-card__btn rdlink__btn" href="https://votercheck.me/rd.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the R&amp;D analysis</a></div></section><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">Highlights</p><div class="project__body"><div class="project__group"><p class="project__group-title">The public search</p><ul class="project__list"><li>Draft rolls for 17 constituencies, about 3.5 million records</li><li>A removed-voter list of about 1.9 million records, for the constituencies where one was published</li><li>Four ways to search: by name and house number, by voter ID, a household view, and against the removed list</li><li>English, Telugu, and Urdu, with voice input and a printable record card</li></ul></div><div class="project__group"><p class="project__group-title">The case system</p><ul class="project__list"><li>Three roles: volunteer, per-constituency coordinator, and administrator, each seeing only what it needs</li><li>A case moves through set states, from submitted on the site to a filed Form 6</li><li>Coordinators assign cases one at a time or in bulk, and each case is locked to a single owner</li><li>Every action is written to an audit trail, and personal details submitted for help are encrypted at rest</li><li>Built to run with hundreds of volunteers and many thousands of cases</li></ul></div><div class="project__group"><p class="project__group-title">Privacy and build</p><ul class="project__list"><li>The search confirms your own record, and shows the full record only after you corroborate identity</li><li>A valid voter ID with the wrong name is not revealed, and no query text or personal data is kept</li><li>The search database and the case database are separate, with separate credentials</li><li>Records came from scanned rolls by OCR, reconciled against each roll's printed totals, and matched across the spelling and word-order variants of a single name</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">How it works</p><div class="project__body"><h2 class="feature__heading">Assistance tracked to a filed Form 6</h2><p>Young Voice of India runs the effort. Volunteers meet people, collect the papers, prepare Form 6, and file it. The case system holds every request in a known state from intake to a filed Form 6.</p><ol class="steps"><li><b>New:</b> a case opens when someone submits from the public site.</li><li><b>Assigned:</b> a coordinator hands it to a volunteer in that constituency.</li><li><b>Contacted:</b> the volunteer reaches out, and every attempt and note is recorded.</li><li><b>Documents received:</b> the papers needed for Form 6 are collected.</li><li><b>Prepared:</b> Form 6 is readied for filing.</li><li><b>Submitted:</b> filed with the election office.</li><li><b>Done:</b> the case is closed once the work is complete.</li></ol><p>A case that stalls is marked could not reach or on hold rather than closed. Roles are scoped so each person sees only what they need. A volunteer works their assigned cases, a per-constituency coordinator triages and assigns within one constituency, and an administrator sees every constituency. People apply to volunteer, and an administrator reviews and approves before access is granted.</p><p>Cases are ownership-gated, so only the assigned volunteer or a coordinator in that constituency can change one. Bulk assignment lets a coordinator move many at once or return them to the pool. Notification badges show unassigned and newly assigned work. Every action is written to an audit trail, including any access to a sensitive field, and personal details submitted for help are encrypted at rest.</p><p>The system is built to run with hundreds of volunteers and many thousands of cases.</p></div></section><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">Stack</p><div class="project__body"><ul class="project__chips"><li class="project__chip">FastAPI</li><li class="project__chip">PostgreSQL</li><li class="project__chip">pg_trgm</li><li class="project__chip">React</li><li class="project__chip">RapidOCR</li><li class="project__chip">Docker</li><li class="project__chip">Cloudflare</li><li class="project__chip">EN / TE / UR</li></ul></div></section><a href="/work" class="project__back project__back--bottom">← Work</a></article>
</BaseLayout>
